initial_review.exact_claim_html:
The first non-trivial Neumann eigenfunction does not have global extrema in the interior of $\Omega$ if
	 	\begin{enumerate}
	 		\item $\Omega\subset \mathbb{R}^2$ is simply connected.
	 		\item $\Omega\subset \mathbb{R}^n$ ($n \ge 3$) is convex.
	 	\end{enumerate}
